; pgBackRest runs as PostgreSQL's archive_command, in PostgreSQL's domain
; postgresql_t, and pushes WAL to S3 over HTTPS (443) with credentials from
; the instance metadata service (80). Both ports are http_port_t. Measured on
; 16 November 2026: without this rule SELinux denies name_connect and
; archiving stops.
;
; This rule is broader than pgBackRest: it lets every process in postgresql_t
; connect to any http_port_t port (80, 443, 8080, ...) on any address,
; including the instance metadata service. Only code running inside
; PostgreSQL can use it; the consumer roles are not superusers. Narrowing it
; to a dedicated pgbackrest_t domain is a follow-up (TAE-138).
(allow postgresql_t http_port_t (tcp_socket (name_connect)))
